/* Bloom: the external symbols of Kvazaar 2.3.2 renamed for its 10-bit build (kvazaar.cmake).
 *
 * Kvazaar fixes its sample depth when it is compiled (KVZ_BIT_DEPTH), so Bloom builds the library
 * twice and links both static archives into one libavcodec: the 8-bit one behind FFmpeg's
 * libkvazaar encoder and the 10-bit one behind libkvazaar10 (dependencies/patches/ffmpeg/0002).
 * Every 10-bit translation unit force-includes this header, which gives each external symbol a
 * kvz10_ prefix, so the two archives never resolve against each other. The FFmpeg wrapper reaches
 * the 10-bit library through <kvazaar10/kvazaar10.h>, which includes this header too.
 *
 * The list is every external symbol of the 8-bit and 10-bit archives (all of them kvz_), plus the
 * POSIX thread, semaphore and getopt replacements Kvazaar compiles only with MSVC. The install
 * step (kvazaar10-install.cmake) refuses an archive that still defines an unprefixed symbol, so a
 * Kvazaar update that adds one fails the build instead of linking silently.
 */
